KERNEL: w90_tenh_lib.tkernel is a copy of x10_stack_lib.skernel (the engine plus ladder, sell penalty, take-profit vs the 24h high and dead-coin cash release) with three new switches:
- cdw: cooldown after a winning exit. cdw=1 means the coin can be bought again at the next hourly check; cd stays the cooldown after a loss.
- liq: a coin whose data ends early (LUNA/FTT/SRM) is sold at its last hour instead of staying frozen at its last price.
- near: bid only on coins whose open is within this distance of the trigger.
w90_tenh_check.py proves it equals engine.run with the switches off: 8 settings x (19 coins, 22 coins) give identical trade logs and 0.0 equity difference, cdw=cd is identical to cdw off, and liq=1 is identical on the 19 coins. It reproduces 10% mode exactly: +15.03 / +8.13 / +6.08 %/month, win rate 81.1 / 76.5 / 75.0%. It also reproduces the live settings: +4.98 / +2.89 / +1.96, win rate 93.6 / 92.5 / 91.5%.
Features are built from closed candles only. Costs: 0.1% fee per side, 0.02% market slippage, limit buys fill only 0.1% through. Spot only and fully funded.

METRICS: %/month is the compounded multiple to the power 1/months. Win rate counts trades bought in the period. Worst trade is trade return x order size / account value.

STRESSED VERSION:
- the real bot's timing: mtp_now=True, cd+1, and cdw+1 (=2), which is slightly harsher than the bot's own 0h re-arm;
- every buy AND sell 0.2% worse;
- LUNA/FTT/SRM added, sold at their last data hour.
The REFINE.md reference stress (bot timing + buys only 0.2% worse) is reported separately in robust.log.

GRIDS (each declared in its script docstring before it ran; every grid looks at 2024-26, so everything is hindsight):
- grid1, 315 designs: N1 x100%, depth 12-16%, take-profit 1.5-8%, time stop 24/48/96h, cooldown 24h, 6h, or 24h with re-arm after a win.
- grid2, 320: per-coin depth tiers by each coin's own 30-day volatility rank (calm third -0 to -6 points, wild third -1 to +2, calm-coin take-profit -2 points), or depth = 2.2-3.4 x the coin's own daily volatility, clipped.
- grid3, 96: crash guard off, or threshold 25-50% with lookback 72/168/336h, on 6 bases.
- grid4, 85:
  - take-profit relative to the 24h high: f 0.25-0.55, on market buys only or on every fill;
  - a second smaller order deeper on the same coin: 60/80% at the trigger, the rest 4/7 points deeper;
  - 2 coins x 50%;
  - 2 orders x 100% with a near-trigger filter of 1/3/6%;
  - cooldown 12/48h with re-arm.
- grid5, 48:
  - extra levers not on the task list: trigger window 12-72h, take-profit placed at the 2nd or 3rd check, no resting take-profit;
  - take-profit relative to the 24h high only;
  - time stop 72/120h;
  - depth +-0.5 point.
- grid6, 146: 1-4 coins x 1/N, depth 12-14%, take-profit 1.5-3%, time stop 48/96h, with or without re-arm. This fills in the win-rate frontier.

Total: 1,010 designs, 943 with distinct results (frontier.log, all_designs.csv).

CHECKS:
- anatomy of 10% mode;
- one-step neighbours, the parts of the stress, 60 fresh start dates and calendar years for 6 candidates (robust.log);
- the stressed version of the top 40 designs;
- replays of a patched copy of panic_buyer.py (+cooldown_after_win_hours) through tests/fake_binance.py, 2021-01-01 to 2026-10-22, on the 16 coins with complete data.
For context, a pick made on 2021-23 only (best 2021-23 %/month in grid1) made +4.3% in 2024-26 and -0.4% since 2025. The top 10 by 2021-23 have a 2024-26 median of 4.8% and a since-2025 median of 2.9%.

UNIVERSE. Core is the user's 19 coins: always eligible, full size, core depth. Tier is the monthly top M of the other screened coins, ranked by trailing 30-day ("v30") or 365-day ("v365") quote volume.
- Ranks are fixed at each month's first hour from past data only: at least 30 days of history, traded in the previous hour.
- Ranks are computed over all 322 screened coins, so none is missed. Delisted coins stay in: 84 of the 299 panel coins stop trading within the data, and LUNA is cut at its collapse.
- The crash guard (skip a coin whose last close is more than 35% under its 168h high close) applies to every coin.

MECHANISM. The live hourly resting-bid bot, not watch mode. Each hour, fully funded limit bids go on the N eligible coins (core or tier) closest to their own trigger. Order size is min(fmax x equity, cash/N) x the tier size multiplier.

KERNEL. w90_wider_lib.wkernel is x10_universe_lib.ukernel (bid branch) plus two switches: a sell penalty, and selling a position at its coin's last data hour. With both off it matches exactly (check.log, "ALL IDENTICAL"):
- engine.run on the 19 coins and on the 22-coin stress panel, 14 settings including 10% mode with the guard;
- x10 urun on the wider panel, 4 cases.
10% mode on the 19 coins reproduces 15.03 / 8.13 / 6.08 %/month.

COSTS. Fee 0.1% per side. Slippage 0.02% for the monthly top 50 by 30-day volume, else 0.1%. Limit buys fill only when the low trades 0.1% through.

STRESSED VERSION. mtp_now=True and cd+1; every buy and sell fill 0.2% worse; LUNA/FTT/SRM forced in as core coins; positions sold at a coin's last data hour.

METRICS. Win rate counts trades bought in the period. %/month is compounded from the continuous 2021 run.

GRIDS (424 designs; 718 grid runs: 424 normal + 294 stressed; about 160 more check runs). Core is 10% mode unless stated.
- grid1: 98 designs, fixed before any result. Ranking v30/v365 x M 30/50 x tier depth 18/20/22% x size 0.5/1 x tier take-profit +5/+8% x N 1/2, plus 19-only controls. 0 qualifiers.
- grid2: 192 designs, hindsight, placed around grid-1 near misses. Ranking x M 20/25/30/40 x tier depth 20/22/24/26% x size 0.5/0.75/1 x a pump filter. 6 qualifiers.
- grid3: 78 designs, hindsight; grid 2's best sat on its edge. Tier depth 24-32%, M 15-40, tier take-profit 5/6/8%, core depth 13/15%, cooldown 12/36h. 15 qualifiers.
- win-rate grid: 56 designs. Take-profit 1.5/2/3% x sizing N8x20% / N3x33% / N1x100% x core 12/14% x tier none / v365 / v30. 29 qualify for 90% win rate, 1 for 10%.

SELECTION RULE (fixed). 10% in both 2021-23 and 2024-26; then the highest worst of (2021-23, 2024-26, since 2025) %/month; ties go to the shallower drop.

LABELLING. The rule sees 2024-26, and grids 2-3 were placed by hindsight, so every qualifier is TUNED ON 2024-26.

CHECKS ON FINALISTS (final.log, robust.log):
- 12 one-step neighbours each;
- fine tier-depth scans in 0.5-point steps;
- core depth scan with and without the tier;
- leaving out the biggest outside-19 coins;
- no new buys on the 10 Oct 2025 flash-crash evening;
- orders that must trade 0.3% or 1% through;
- fresh starts;
- the holdout functions run through the holdout_eval path.

